  "function_revised": "Mce-associated membrane (Mam) protein OmamA (orphaned Mam protein A), an exported virulence factor that stabilises the Mce lipid-transport complexes. RefSeq leaves this locus 'hypothetical protein'; here it is re-annotated from published genetics/cell biology. Rv0199 is required for cholesterol import (a Mce4-dependent process) and stabilises protein components of the Mce1 transporter complex, a role proposed to be analogous to VirB8 in stabilising Type-IV secretion systems (Perkowski 2016). It was independently identified as an exported, intracellular-growth factor (β-lactamase reporter transposon screen; attenuated macrophage growth) (McCann 2011). Experimentally characterised, not a structural prediction.",
